  <!-- ===============================================================
       PAST MISSIONS

       A carousel: it scrolls on its own and can also be dragged,
       swiped, or stepped through with the arrows and dots.
       Behaviour is in assets/js/carousel.js; the dots are generated
       there, so adding a card here needs no other change.
       Change data-carousel-interval to speed it up or slow it down.
       =============================================================== -->
  <section class="section section--muted" id="archive">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="eyebrow">Archive</span>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <h2>Past missions.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Earlier project teams, and the International Aerial Robotics
          Competition missions we flew against top universities from around
          the world.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="carousel" data-carousel data-carousel-interval="5000">
        <div
          class="carousel__track"
          tabindex="0"
          role="region"
          aria-label="Past missions"
        >
          <article class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">
              <span class="icon icon--package icon--lg" aria-hidden="true"
              ></span>
            </span>
            <p class="card__index">2025 &ndash; 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card__title">Claw Retrieval</h3>
            <p class="card__body">
              A drone for autonomous object retrieval and delivery using a
              claw mechanism. The team designed a 2-in-1 landing gear and
              claw system for payload handling, a driver PCB controlling a
              stepper motor for the claw using PID control, and a
              searchlight to allow operation in low-light conditions.
            </p>
            <div class="card__spacer"></div>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li class="tag">PID control</li>
              <li class="tag">Driver PCB</li>
              <li class="tag">Landing gear</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">
              <span class="icon icon--target icon--lg" aria-hidden="true"
              ></span>
            </span>
            <p class="card__index">2025 &ndash; 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card__title">Thrust Vector Control Dart</h3>
            <p class="card__body">
              A drone system capable of deploying a dart with thrust
              vectoring control via a coaxial motor for precise
              manoeuvrability. The dart, controlled by an ESP32
              microcontroller, carried a camera for real-time video
              streaming and self-landed on deployment, released by a
              servo-driven mechanism.
            </p>
            <div class="card__spacer"></div>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li class="tag">Thrust vectoring</li>
              <li class="tag">ESP32</li>
              <li class="tag">Video streaming</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">
              <span class="icon icon--eye icon--lg" aria-hidden="true"
              ></span>
            </span>
            <p class="card__index">2025 &ndash; 2026</p>
            <h3 class="card__title">Color Vision Targeting</h3>
            <p class="card__body">
              A fully autonomous Nerf gun drone system capable of detecting
              and targeting maroon-coloured objects, combining image
              recognition, autonomous navigation, and rapid-fire mechanisms
              to hit specific objects with precision.
            </p>
            <div class="card__spacer"></div>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li class="tag">Object detection</li>
              <li class="tag">Image recognition</li>
              <li class="tag">Drone control</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">
              <span class="icon icon--route icon--lg" aria-hidden="true"
              ></span>
            </span>
            <p class="card__index">IARC Mission 7</p>
            <h3 class="card__title">Herding autonomous ground robots</h3>
            <p class="card__body">
              Mission 7 took a monumental leap by requiring autonomous
              aerial robots to interact with and control autonomous ground
              robots. Teams were tasked with developing systems to herd
              ground robots out one end of an arena in the absence of 3D
              cues such as walls. The ground robots could only be
              interacted with by touch: a top touch commanded a 45&deg;
              clockwise turn, and a blocking action resulted in a 180&deg;
              turn.
            </p>
            <div class="card__spacer"></div>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li class="tag">YOLO</li>
              <li class="tag">ArduCopter</li>
              <li class="tag">EKF</li>
              <li class="tag">2D LiDAR</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">
              <span class="icon icon--swarm icon--lg" aria-hidden="true"
              ></span>
            </span>
            <p class="card__index">IARC Mission 8</p>
            <h3 class="card__title">Swarm control without GPS</h3>
            <p class="card__body">
              For 2019, IARC changed missions. Mission 8 was again designed
              to challenge the bounds of what was currently possible in
              aerial robotics. Teams had to control a swarm of drones,
              which accepted commands via audio or visual input rather than
              a traditional radio controller: read and process four
              fragments of a QR code, piece them together to unlock a
              chest, and avoid both enemy drones and arena obstacles. This
              mission was also GPS denied.
            </p>
            <div class="card__spacer"></div>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li class="tag">Swarms</li>
              <li class="tag">Obstacle avoidance</li>
              <li class="tag">QR decoding</li>
              <li class="tag">GPS denied</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <span class="card__icon">
              <span class="icon icon--trophy icon--lg" aria-hidden="true"
              ></span>
            </span>
            <p class="card__index">IARC Mission 9</p>
            <h3 class="card__title">Repairing a moving platform</h3>
            <p class="card__body">
              Our drone had to fly approximately two miles from the
              starting location, around pylons, to a mast simulating the
              movement of a ship at sea. Once there, it had to synchronise
              with the mast, remove a defective communications module,
              replace it with a good one, and return to the starting
              location &mdash; in under nine minutes, using only onboard
              computing.
            </p>
            <div class="card__spacer"></div>
            <ul class="tags">
              <li class="tag">Precision manipulation</li>
              <li class="tag">Moving frames</li>
              <li class="tag">Optical recognition</li>
              <li class="tag">Onboard compute</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="carousel__controls">
          <button
            class="carousel__button carousel__button--prev"
            type="button"
            data-carousel-prev
            aria-label="Previous past missions"
          >
            <span class="icon icon--chevron-left" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>

          <div class="carousel__dots" data-carousel-dots></div>

          <button
            class="carousel__button carousel__button--next"
            type="button"
            data-carousel-next
            aria-label="Next past missions"
          >
            <span
              class="icon icon--chevron-right"
              aria-hidden="true"
            ></span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

